{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfxo7sB63DLdNjrg5EcaK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four steps are done, and I read the rule back to confirm it's enabled.\n\n- **Data view:** the time field is `timestamp`.\n- **Dashboard:** \"S4-4af67afb Web logs\" has two panels. The first is \"Requests over time\" and the second, after the rename, is \"Responses by code\". I read the dashboard back and the new title is in place.\n- **Alert rule:** \"S4-4af67afb 5xx errors\" (id `8f141bd8-b2b9-4b6a-bfd4-6c758b5e2a59`) checks every minute. It fires when more than 10 requests with a response code from 500 to 599 arrive within 5 minutes. It was created disabled, so I enabled it, and the read-back shows it enabled with status \"ok\".\n- **Range match:** `response` is a string field, so the rule matches codes 500–599 as a string range on `response.keyword`. That covers every three-digit code in that range.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":537,"cache_read_input_tokens":20788,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":537},"output_tokens":332,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0da1e72d-e9d9-58d9-b388-fca8d0eba393","uuid":"c1ab245a-3bcb-4d4c-bb82-01741ae0a5e0","timestamp":"2026-10-12T18:12:56.116Z","request_id":"req_011Cfxo7rtjR7JuKfRvfXXsH"}
